# ── Runtime server artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
cs_server.log
save_game_*.dat
save_gov_*.dat
server/*.sqlite3
server/.venv/
# captured savegame blobs, and the blob loadgame injects when present
server/saves/
server/loadgame_blob.b64
# raw blobs handed to the client as its command-line argument at startup
client/*.dat
# ...except the Single Player galaxy, which is not a throwaway capture but a
# shipped release asset: build.ps1 copies it into the zip, so a checkout without
# it cannot build a release at all.
!client/SinglePlayerGalaxy.dat

# ── Build / debug leftovers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.hex
*.log
*.dmp
__pycache__/

# ── Dev tool output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
client/dev_tools/snapshots/
# the AI's persistent fog-of-war map: per machine, per galaxy, per civ — game
# state rather than source, and meaningless in another checkout
client/dev_tools/ai_player/state/
*.exe.bak
tools

# named restore points (raw save blobs, big and regenerable)
client/checkpoints/
.vscode

# ── Release build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The staged release folder duplicates the 8 MB client binaries that are already
# tracked in client/ — it is an artifact of release/build.ps1, regenerable from
# the manifest, and belongs on a GitHub release rather than in the history.
dist/
release/build/
release/.venv-build/
# written by launcher.py when it is run from a checkout rather than a release
release/data/
